     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §385, V & T L",
    "lawSection": "Vehicle and Traffic Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S4278\n\nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the vehicle and traffic law, in\nrelation to exempting fire vehicles from the weight restrictions of\nother vehicles\n\nPURPOSE:  This bill would allow fire departments to legally operate\napparatus being used for the purpose of public safety, but which\nviolate New York's weight restrictions\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. Adds a new subdivision 23 to section 385 of the vehicle and\ntraffic law to exempt fire vehicles from the weight restrictions of\nother vehicles\n\nSection 2 is the effective date.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:  New York is one of only several states which do not\nspecifically exempt fire vehicles from weight restrictions under the\nvehicle and traffic law. This has caused fire departments to either\nknowingly disregard the laws to operate necessary emergency vehicles\nor purchase vehicles that are inadequate in order to adhere to the\nlegal weight restrictions. Currently, an average tandem axle Tower\nLadder will weigh approximately 80,000 pounds. These vehicles are\nbeing operated out of compliance on a daily basis.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:  New bill\n\nFISCAL IMPACT ON THE STATE: None.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:  This act shall take immediately.\n\n",
    "multiSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
