    "lawCode": "Amd §385, V & T L",
    "lawSection": "Vehicle and Traffic Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S4278A\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the vehicle and traffic law, in relation to exempting\nfire vehicles from the weight restrictions of other vehicles\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the vehicle and traffic law, in relation to exempting\nfire vehicles from the weight restrictions of other vehicles\n\nPURPOSE:\n\nThis bill would allow fire departments to legally operate apparatus\nbeing used for the purpose of public safety, but which violate New\nYork's weight restrictions\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. Adds a new subdivision 23 to section 385 of the vehicle and\ntraffic law to exempt fire vehicles from the certain weight and\ndimension restrictions, except those weight and height restrictions\nthat are posted over, on or through any bridge or structure on any\nhighway.\n\nSection 2 is the effective date.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nNew York is one of only several states which do not specifically\nexempt fire vehicles from weight restrictions under the vehicle and\ntraffic law. This has caused fire departments to either knowingly\ndisregard the laws to operate necessary emergency vehicles or purchase\nvehicles that are inadequate in order to adhere to the legal weight\nrestrictions. Currently, an average tandem axle Tower Ladder will\nweigh approximately 80,000 pounds. These vehicles are being operated\nout of compliance on a daily basis.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill\n\nFISCAL IMPACT ON THE STATE:\n\nNone.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\n\nThis act shall take immediately.\n\n",
